      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "description": "How to read this dashboard.",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### cert-manager: TLS certificates for the lab\n**What it does here.** Issues the wildcard certificate `*.staffops.space` (Certificate `gateway/wildcard`, ClusterIssuer\n`letsencrypt-prod`, ACME DNS-01 on Cloudflare with the token from Vault) used by the Gateway for every HTTPS hostname, plus\nthe self-signed serving certificate of the OpenTelemetry operator webhook. The **webhook** validates cert-manager\nobjects; **cainjector** injects CA bundles into webhook configurations.\n\n**The key questions:** is every certificate Ready, how long until the soonest expiry, did the last renewal work, is\nLet's Encrypt answering (no 429 rate limits)? Let's Encrypt certificates live 90 days and cert-manager renews them 30\ndays before expiry, so *time to expiry* should never go below ~30 days. If it does, the renewal is failing.\n\n**When something is red:** `kubectl --context k8s01 describe certificate -n gateway wildcard`, then the latest\n`CertificateRequest`/`Order`/`Challenge` (`kubectl --context k8s01 get certificaterequests,orders,challenges -A`) and the\ncontroller logs (`kubectl --context k8s01 -n cert-manager logs deploy/cert-manager`). DNS-01 failures are usually the\nCloudflare token (ExternalSecret `cert-manager/cloudflare-api-token` → see the External Secrets and Vault dashboards).\nAlerts: `CertificateNotReady` (30m), `CertificateExpiringSoon` (< 14 days). Docs: [mixin](https://github.com/imusmanmalik/cert-manager-mixin),\n[cert-manager metrics](https://cert-manager.io/docs/devops-tips/prometheus-metrics/).",
        "code": {
          "language": "markdown",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        }
      },
      "id": 1,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 9
      }
    },
